#!/usr/bin/env -S python3 -I
"""local-review: run Codex's code review LOCALLY on the exact head of a PR and file the result for `pr-wait --local-codex`.

  local-review PR [--repo OWNER/NAME] [--head SHA] [--timeout S] [--allow-untrusted] [--json]

Why (2026-10-29, operator: "could we just switch to making codex reviews run locally in general"): the GitHub Codex review of PRs 112 and 124 sat
"Running" until the waiter gave up (openai/codex#55890), while `codex review --base origin/master` run by hand finished in 2.3-11 minutes (the machine's load)
at about 0.3% of the weekly Codex quota and found real P1/P2 bugs on every run. This makes that run a step with a recorded, head-bound result, so a merge no
longer waits on a bot that may never answer. Run it AFTER the push has landed (the PR's head comes from the GitHub API, which can lag a push by seconds).

What it does, from a checkout of the repo (any worktree; it fetches into its object store and adds one temporary linked worktree under the state dir,
and touches nothing else of yours):
  1. asks `gh api repos/R/pulls/N` for the PR's head and base (`--head SHA` pins a head, which must be the PR's current head or one of its ancestors), then
     fetches the base and `refs/pull/N/head` so both commits are present locally;
  2. adds a CLEAN, DETACHED worktree at exactly that head under the state dir (nothing of yours is reviewed: no dirty file, no other branch);
  3. runs `codex review --base <base_sha>` there (the base branch's tip, resolved once after the fetch and pinned by SHA, so a moving origin/<base> cannot change what is reviewed) with a read-only sandbox and a scrubbed environment (no token, secret or password variable, no GH_/GITHUB_
     variable), stdout and stderr kept as <stem>.out and <stem>.err, the whole process group killed after --timeout seconds (default 1500) and again when codex
     exits, so nothing survives it;
  4. reads the findings from Codex's FINAL message (`- [P0..P3] title - path:lines`), removes the worktree and files
     $LOCAL_REVIEW_STATE_DIR (default ~/.local/state/local-review)/<owner>__<name>-pr<N>-<head>.json, atomically, 0600 in a 0700 directory.
The result document (schema 1): repo, pr, head, base_ref, base_sha, result (clean | findings | failed), reason (failed only), exit_code, final_message
(bool), counts {P0..P3}, findings [{priority, title, path}] (titles only: the finding text stays in <stem>.out), ignored_generated, dirty_after, codex
version, started/finished, elapsed_s, and the sha256 of the output files. It is written as `failed: in progress` the moment the lock is taken, so a run that dies
leaves no older `clean` behind.

Rules (each one a way a local review could lie, so each is pinned by a test):
  1. FAIL CLOSED. `clean` needs exit 0, a final message on stdout that EQUALS (whitespace folded) the last `codex` block of the stderr transcript, POSITIVE evidence
     that this run was reviewed as asked (the transcript's `workdir:`, `sandbox: read-only` and `changes against '<base_sha>'` lines, and an `exec` block; a refusal blacklist alone misses wordings), no message that reads as a refusal,
     and zero parsed findings. Codex not installed, a timeout, a non-zero
     exit, no final message, a stdout that is not the transcript's final message, a head that moved under the worktree, and any line that looks
     like a finding but is not exactly `- [P0..P3] ...` (a format change: `**[P1]**`, `[P1]`, `P1:`, a bullet `*`) are all `failed`, never `clean`.
  2. THE HEAD IS THE KEY. The file name and its `head` field are the full 40-hex head that was reviewed; `pr-wait` reads only that name and re-checks the field,
     the PR and the base, so a review of an older head or another base is never read. Pushing a fix means running this again (the review is the cost).
  3. GENERATED FILES ARE NOT THE PR. The graft hook rewrites tracked `.cursor/hooks.json` and `.claude/settings.json` in any worktree it runs in; a finding
     located in such a file that is dirty in the review worktree afterwards AND that the PR itself does not change is recorded under `ignored_generated`, not
     counted. A finding on a hook file the PR edits always counts.
  4. NOTHING IS POSTED. No comment, no review, no label: the result is a local file only a same-user process can write. Quote the summary line in the PR body.
  5. ONE RUN PER HEAD AT A TIME: a flock on a lock file, released when the process dies (no stale lock) and only AFTER the result is published, so another run's
     `in progress` record is never overwritten by an older verdict; a second run exits 4.
  6. THE VERDICT TEXT IS PROSE. Whether a no-findings message is a completed review is decided by the structural bindings of rule 1 (transcript header, `exec`, equal
     channels) plus a refusal wording list scoped to the review itself; no list is complete, so an unusual refusal worded around it after a bound transcript with an
     `exec` block can still read clean. A false `failed` costs a rerun; read the `.out` of a clean result when a merge matters.
  7. THE REVIEWED TREE IS UNTRUSTED INPUT, SO THE AUTHOR MUST BE TRUSTED (Codex Security Review on PR 130). Codex runs as you, in a worktree of the PR, with a read-only sandbox, no network and no token in its environment (the files in your home stay readable by the model); a diff or an AGENTS.md in
     the PR can still try to talk the model into "no issues", as it can the GitHub bot. A PR whose author is neither the repository owner nor the authenticated gh user is refused (exit 2) unless --allow-untrusted.
     Residual: a tool process that is reparented to init between two 2-second looks AND works outside the worktree escapes (no cgroups on macOS).

Exit: 0 clean, 1 findings, 2 usage / no such PR / not in a checkout of that repo / an author that is not trusted, 3 failed (see `reason` in the file and on stderr), 4 another run for the
same head is alive.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import fcntl
import hashlib
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from datetime import datetime, timezone
from pathlib import Path

DEFAULT_REPO = "djbclark/djbclark-ade"
SCHEMA = 1
PRIORITIES = ("P0", "P1", "P2", "P3")
FINDING_RE = re.compile(r"^- \[(P[0-3])\]\s+(\S.*)$")
# anything that looks like a finding but is not exactly the line above: if one is seen the parse is wrong, never "no findings"
FINDING_SHAPED_RE = re.compile(r"(?i)\[\s*P\s*\d\s*\]|^\W*P\d\b|\*\*\s*P\d")
# Wording of a review that did NOT happen. Narrow on purpose (round 8): it only fires on inability to review/inspect/read/finish, or on an abort, a size or
# context limit, a denied or blocked sandbox. "I could not run tests" and "the patch fixes the failed command" are ordinary summaries of a finished review.
INABILITY = r"(?:unable|not able|(?:wasn|weren)'?t able|could ?n[o']t|can ?n[o']t|failed|(?:didn'?t|did not) (?:finish|complete))"
UNDONE = r"(?:review\w*|complet\w*|finish\w*|inspect\w*|access\w*|read(?!-)|load\w*)"
STATE = r"(?:aborted|incomplete|partial|blocked|failed|stopped|cut short|unavailable|inaccessible)"
REFUSAL_RE = re.compile(
    rf"(?i)\b{INABILITY}\s+(?:to\s+)?(?:\w+\s+){{0,2}}{UNDONE}\b"    # "I wasn't able to review the patch"
    rf"|\b(?:review|analysis|inspection)\b[^.\n]{{0,25}}\b{STATE}\b"    # "the review was incomplete"; never a bare "incomplete records"
    rf"|\b(?:repository|repo|checkout|worktree|diff|patch)\b[^.\n]{{0,15}}\b(?:inaccessible|unavailable)\b"    # "the repository is unavailable"
    r"|\b(?:stopped early|cut short|ran out of (?:context|budget|tokens)|nothing was reviewed|not reviewed|partial review|too large to review|"
    r"context window (?:was )?exhausted|denied access|blocked (?:every|all))\b|not logged in|codex login")
GENERATED = (".cursor/hooks.json", ".claude/settings.json")
SECRET_ENV_RE = re.compile(r"(?i)(token|secret|passw|credential|api_?key)|^(GH|GITHUB)_")
KEEP_ENV_RE = re.compile(r"^(CODEX_|OPENAI_)")
GH_TIMEOUT = int(os.environ.get("LOCAL_REVIEW_GH_TIMEOUT") or 90)    # seconds for the one `gh api` call (overridable so a test need not wait 90)
GIT_TIMEOUT = 300
EXIT_CLEAN, EXIT_FINDINGS, EXIT_USAGE, EXIT_FAILED, EXIT_DUP = 0, 1, 2, 3, 4


def state_dir() -> Path:
    return Path(os.environ.get("LOCAL_REVIEW_STATE_DIR") or Path.home() / ".local/state/local-review")


def run(argv: list[str], *, cwd: str | None = None, timeout: int = GIT_TIMEOUT) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:
    return subprocess.run(argv, cwd=cwd, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)


def now_iso() -> str:
    return datetime.now(timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def fold(text: str) -> str:
    return " ".join(text.split())


def parse_findings(message: str) -> tuple[list[dict], bool]:
    """([{priority, title, path}], parsed_everything). A line that looks like a finding but is not exactly one makes `parsed_everything` False."""
    seen: set[str] = set()
    out: list[dict] = []
    parsed_everything = True
    for line in message.splitlines():
        m = FINDING_RE.match(line)
        if not m:
            if FINDING_SHAPED_RE.search(line) and not line.lstrip().startswith("- [Positive"):
                parsed_everything = False
            continue
        if line in seen:
            continue
        seen.add(line)
        title, path = m.group(2), ""
        if " \u2014 " in title:    # `title \u2014 path:lines`, the last separator
            title, _, path = title.rpartition(" \u2014 ")
        out.append({"priority": m.group(1), "title": title.strip(), "path": path.strip()})
    return out, parsed_everything


def final_message(out_text: str, err_text: str) -> tuple[str, str]:
    """(message, problem). The final review is stdout; it must equal, whitespace folded, the last `codex` block of the stderr transcript, which is how a
    review is told from an error message or a banner that happens to exit 0."""
    if not out_text.strip():
        return "", "codex printed no final message"
    blocks = re.split(r"(?m)^codex$", err_text)
    if len(blocks) < 2:
        return "", "the transcript has no `codex` message block, so stdout cannot be shown to be a review"
    if fold(blocks[-1]) != fold(out_text):
        return "", "stdout is not the transcript's final message"
    return out_text, ""


def is_generated(finding_path: str, dirty: set[str], pr_files: set[str], root: str) -> bool:
    p = finding_path.split(":", 1)[0] if finding_path else ""
    if not p:
        return False
    rel = os.path.relpath(p, root) if os.path.isabs(p) else p
    return rel in GENERATED and rel in dirty and rel not in pr_files


def sha256_file(path: Path) -> str:
    return hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()


def write_private(path: Path, text: str) -> None:
    tmp = path.with_name(f"{path.name}.tmp.{os.getpid()}")
    fd = os.open(tmp, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC, 0o600)
    with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
        f.write(text)
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def take_lock(path: Path) -> int | None:
    """An exclusive flock on PATH, held (the returned fd) until this process ends; None when another run holds it."""
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT, 0o600)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except BlockingIOError:
        os.close(fd)
        return None
    os.ftruncate(fd, 0)
    os.write(fd, str(os.getpid()).encode())
    return fd


def die(msg: str, code: int) -> int:
    print(f"local-review: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
    return code


def build_parser() -> argparse.ArgumentParser:
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="local-review", description="Run Codex's code review locally on the exact head of a PR "
                                "and file the result for `pr-wait --local-codex`. Exit: 0 clean, 1 findings, 2 usage, 3 failed, 4 duplicate.")
    p.add_argument("pr", type=int, help="pull request number")
    p.add_argument("--repo", default=DEFAULT_REPO, help=f"OWNER/NAME (default {DEFAULT_REPO})")
    p.add_argument("--head", help="the full head SHA to review (default: the PR's current head)")
    p.add_argument("--allow-untrusted", action="store_true", help="review a PR whose author is neither the repository owner nor the authenticated gh user "
                   "(its diff and AGENTS.md can steer the reviewing model)")
    p.add_argument("--timeout", type=int, default=1500, help="seconds before codex is killed (default 1500)")
    p.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", help="print the result document as one JSON line")
    return p


def codex_env() -> dict[str, str]:
    """The environment codex runs in: no token, secret, password or GH_/GITHUB_ variable (codex's own CODEX_/OPENAI_ ones stay)."""
    return {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if KEEP_ENV_RE.match(k) or not SECRET_ENV_RE.search(k)}


def mask_signals() -> None:
    """From here on nothing may cut the cleanup or the publish short: a SIGTERM there would leave codex's tool processes, the worktree or a stale result."""
    for sig in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP, signal.SIGINT):
        signal.signal(sig, signal.SIG_IGN)


class Interrupted(Exception):
    pass


def on_signal(signum: int, _frame: object) -> None:
    raise Interrupted(f"interrupted by signal {signum}")


def main(argv: list[str]) -> int:
    a = build_parser().parse_args(argv)
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[\w.-]+/[\w.-]+", a.repo):
        return die(f"--repo must be OWNER/NAME, got '{a.repo}'", EXIT_USAGE)
    a.repo = a.repo.lower()    # one identity for the file name, the lock, the stored field and the reader (GitHub names are case-insensitive)
    if a.pr < 1 or a.timeout < 1:
        return die("PR and --timeout must be positive", EXIT_USAGE)
    if a.head is not None and not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{40}", a.head):
        return die(f"--head must be a full lowercase 40-hex SHA, got '{a.head}'", EXIT_USAGE)

    top = run(["git", "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel"])
    if top.returncode != 0:
        return die("run it from a checkout of the repository", EXIT_USAGE)
    root = top.stdout.strip()
    origin = run(["git", "remote", "get-url", "origin"], cwd=root).stdout.strip()
    if "/".join(re.split(r"[/:]", origin.removesuffix(".git").rstrip("/"))[-2:]).lower() != a.repo.lower():    # the whole owner/name, never a substring
        return die(f"origin of {root} is {origin!r}, not {a.repo}", EXIT_USAGE)

    gh = run(["gh", "api", f"repos/{a.repo}/pulls/{a.pr}"], timeout=GH_TIMEOUT)
    if gh.returncode != 0:
        return die(f"gh api pulls/{a.pr} failed: {gh.stderr.strip()[:200]}", EXIT_USAGE)
    try:
        doc = json.loads(gh.stdout)
        pr_head, base = doc["head"]["sha"], doc["base"]["ref"]
    except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
        return die("unexpected pulls document", EXIT_USAGE)
    author = ((doc.get("user") or {}).get("login") or "") if isinstance(doc, dict) else ""
    trusted = {a.repo.split("/")[0].lower()}
    me = run(["gh", "api", "user"], timeout=GH_TIMEOUT)
    if me.returncode == 0:
        try:
            trusted.add(str(json.loads(me.stdout).get("login") or "").lower())
        except (ValueError, AttributeError):
            pass
    trusted.discard("")
    if author.lower() not in trusted and not a.allow_untrusted:
        # The reviewed tree is the PR's: its AGENTS.md and diff can talk the model into "no issues" (Codex Security Review on PR 130). A merge gate
        # built on that reading is only as good as the author, so a stranger's PR is refused unless the operator says otherwise.
        return die(f"the PR's author {author or '(unknown)'!r} is neither the repository owner nor the authenticated gh user: its diff and AGENTS.md can steer the "
                   "reviewing model; --allow-untrusted reviews it anyway", EXIT_USAGE)
    head = a.head or pr_head
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{40}", head or "") or not re.fullmatch(r"[\w./-]+", base or ""):
        return die(f"the PR's head or base is not usable: {head!r} / {base!r}", EXIT_USAGE)

    sd = state_dir()
    try:
        sd.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True, mode=0o700)
        os.chmod(sd, 0o700)
    except OSError as e:
        return die(f"cannot use the state directory {sd}: {e}", EXIT_FAILED)
    stem = f"{a.repo.replace('/', '__')}-pr{a.pr}-{head}"
    result_path, out_path, err_path = sd / f"{stem}.json", sd / f"{stem}.out", sd / f"{stem}.err"
    lock_fd = take_lock(sd / f"lock-{stem}")
    if lock_fd is None:
        return die(f"another local-review for {head[:12]} is running (see {sd / f'lock-{stem}'})", EXIT_DUP)

    started, t0 = now_iso(), time.monotonic()
    doc_out: dict = {"schema": SCHEMA, "repo": a.repo, "pr": a.pr, "head": head, "author": author, "base_ref": base, "base_sha": "", "result": "failed",
                     "reason": "in progress (a run that died leaves this)", "exit_code": None, "final_message": False,
                     "counts": {k: 0 for k in PRIORITIES}, "findings": [], "ignored_generated": [], "dirty_after": [],
                     "codex_version": "", "started": started, "finished": "", "elapsed_s": 0.0, "out_sha256": "", "err_sha256": ""}
    write_private(result_path, json.dumps(doc_out, indent=1) + "\n")    # an older `clean` for this head must not survive a run that dies
    for sig in (signal.SIGTERM, signal.SIGHUP):
        signal.signal(sig, on_signal)
    wt = sd / "wt" / f"{stem[-12:]}-{os.getpid()}"
    worktree_added = False
    doc_out["reason"] = ""
    try:
        try:
            fetch = run(["git", "fetch", "-q", "origin", f"refs/pull/{a.pr}/head"], cwd=root)
            if fetch.returncode != 0:
                raise RuntimeError(f"git fetch failed: {fetch.stderr.strip()[:200]}")
            if run(["git", "cat-file", "-e", f"{head}^{{commit}}"], cwd=root).returncode != 0:
                raise RuntimeError(f"commit {head[:12]} is not in the repository after fetching the PR")
            if head != pr_head and run(["git", "merge-base", "--is-ancestor", head, pr_head], cwd=root).returncode != 0:
                return finish(doc_out, result_path, t0, a.json, usage_error=f"--head {head[:12]} is neither the PR's head {pr_head[:12]} nor one of its ancestors")
            if head != pr_head:
                print(f"local-review: note: {head[:12]} is not the PR's current head {pr_head[:12]}; the result names {head[:12]}", file=sys.stderr)
            # the base branch's tip, fetched into a ref of our own and read from it: FETCH_HEAD is shared state another `git fetch` in the same repository
            # overwrites, and a single-branch clone has no origin/<base> to read
            ref = f"refs/local-review/base-{os.getpid()}"
            bfetch = run(["git", "fetch", "-q", "origin", f"+refs/heads/{base}:{ref}"], cwd=root)
            base_sha = run(["git", "rev-parse", "--verify", f"{ref}^{{commit}}"], cwd=root).stdout.strip() if bfetch.returncode == 0 else ""
            run(["git", "update-ref", "-d", ref], cwd=root)    # the commit stays in the object store; the ref was only a pin for the read
            if not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{40}", base_sha):
                raise RuntimeError(f"cannot fetch the base branch {base}: {bfetch.stderr.strip()[:200]}")
            doc_out["base_sha"] = base_sha
            wt.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True, mode=0o700)
            worktree_added = True    # BEFORE the add: an interrupt in the middle of a checkout still gets its half-made worktree removed and pruned
            add = run(["git", "worktree", "add", "--detach", str(wt), head], cwd=root)
            if add.returncode != 0:
                raise RuntimeError(f"git worktree add failed: {add.stderr.strip()[:200]}")
            try:
                doc_out["codex_version"] = (run(["codex", "--version"], timeout=20).stdout.strip().splitlines() or [""])[0][:80]
            except FileNotFoundError:
                raise RuntimeError("codex is not installed (no `codex` on PATH)") from None
            doc_out.update(review(wt, root, base, base_sha, out_path, err_path, a.timeout, head))
        except (Interrupted, KeyboardInterrupt) as e:
            doc_out["reason"] = str(e) or "interrupted"
        except FileNotFoundError as e:
            doc_out["reason"] = f"{e.filename or 'a required program'} not found"
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as e:
            doc_out["reason"] = f"{' '.join(map(str, e.cmd[:3]))} timed out"
        except (RuntimeError, OSError) as e:
            doc_out["reason"] = str(e)
        except Exception as e:    # any other fault is a failed review, never a traceback with exit 1 (which reads as "findings")
            doc_out["reason"] = f"{type(e).__name__}: {e}"
    finally:
        mask_signals()
        if worktree_added:
            rm = run(["git", "worktree", "remove", "--force", str(wt)], cwd=root)
            if rm.returncode != 0:
                shutil.rmtree(wt, ignore_errors=True)
                run(["git", "worktree", "prune"], cwd=root)
    try:
        return finish(doc_out, result_path, t0, a.json)
    finally:
        os.close(lock_fd)    # released only after the result is published: another run's `in progress` record can never be overwritten by this older verdict


def review(wt: Path, root: str, base: str, base_sha: str, out_path: Path, err_path: Path, timeout: int, head: str) -> dict:
    """Run codex in the worktree and return the fields to merge into the result document."""
    res: dict = {}
    proc = None
    with open(out_path, "wb") as out_f, open(err_path, "wb") as err_f:
        try:
            proc = subprocess.Popen(["codex", "review", "-c", 'sandbox_mode="read-only"', "--base", base_sha], cwd=str(wt), stdout=out_f,
                                    stderr=err_f, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, start_new_session=True, env=codex_env())
        except FileNotFoundError:
            return {"reason": "codex is not installed (no `codex` on PATH)"}
        tracked: dict[int, str] = {}
        deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout
        try:
            while not exited(proc):    # poll, so the descendants are SEEN while codex is alive (they are reparented, and untraceable, once it exits)
                if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
                    return {"reason": f"codex did not finish in {timeout} s", "exit_code": None}
                try:
                    tracked.update(descendants(proc.pid))
                except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
                    pass
                time.sleep(min(1.0, max(0.05, deadline - time.monotonic())))
        finally:
            kill_group(proc, wt, tracked)    # on every exit of the wait, including an interrupt: nothing of codex's survives it
    code = proc.returncode
    res["exit_code"] = code
    res["out_sha256"], res["err_sha256"] = sha256_file(out_path), sha256_file(err_path)
    status = run(["git", "status", "--porcelain"], cwd=str(wt))
    dirty = sorted({ln[3:].strip().strip('"') for ln in status.stdout.splitlines() if len(ln) > 3})
    res["dirty_after"] = dirty
    now_head = run(["git", "rev-parse", "HEAD"], cwd=str(wt)).stdout.strip()
    if now_head != head:
        res["reason"] = f"the worktree head moved from {head[:12]} to {now_head[:12]} during the review"
        return res
    if code != 0:
        res["reason"] = f"codex exited {code}"
        return res
    msg, problem = final_message(out_path.read_text(errors="replace"), err_path.read_text(errors="replace"))
    res["final_message"] = bool(msg.strip())
    if problem:
        res["reason"] = problem
        return res
    findings, parsed_all = parse_findings(msg)
    if not parsed_all:
        res["reason"] = "the final message holds finding-shaped lines this parser cannot read (a format change?)"
        return res
    transcript = err_path.read_text(errors="replace")
    bound = (any(re.search(rf"(?m)^workdir: {re.escape(w)}$", transcript) for w in {str(wt), str(wt.resolve())}) and re.search(r"(?m)^sandbox: read-only$", transcript)
             and re.search(rf"(?m)^user\nchanges against '{base_sha}'$", transcript))
    if not bound:
        res["reason"] = "the transcript does not show the review this run asked for (workdir, a read-only sandbox, a diff against the pinned base)"
        return res
    diff = run(["git", "diff", "--name-only", f"{base_sha}...{head}"], cwd=root)
    if diff.returncode != 0:
        res["reason"] = f"cannot list the files the PR changes: {diff.stderr.strip()[:150]}"
        return res
    pr_files = set(diff.stdout.splitlines())
    dirty_set = set(dirty)
    kept, ignored = [], []
    for f in findings:
        (ignored if is_generated(f["path"], dirty_set, pr_files, str(wt)) else kept).append(f)
    if not kept and (REFUSAL_RE.search(msg) or msg.rstrip().endswith("?") or not re.search(r"(?m)^exec$", transcript)):
        # Nothing left to report is a verdict only when the transcript shows codex looked at the repository (an `exec` block) and the message is no
        # refusal. Judged AFTER the generated-file filter: an incomplete review that mentions one ignored hook finding is still incomplete (Codex, round 7)
        res["reason"] = "no findings, but the final message reads as a refusal or the transcript shows no repository inspection: not a verdict"
        return res
    res["findings"], res["ignored_generated"] = kept, ignored
    res["counts"] = {k: sum(1 for f in kept if f["priority"] == k) for k in PRIORITIES}
    res["result"] = "findings" if kept else "clean"
    return res


def exited(proc: subprocess.Popen) -> bool:
    """True once codex has exited, WITHOUT reaping it where the OS allows (waitid + WNOWAIT): an unreaped leader keeps its process group, so a child
    launched just before the exit is still killed by the group kill even where neither lsof nor a snapshot finds it (Codex, GitHub review of PR 130)."""
    if hasattr(os, "waitid"):
        return os.waitid(os.P_PID, proc.pid, os.WEXITED | os.WNOHANG | os.WNOWAIT) is not None
    return proc.poll() is not None


def descendants(pid: int) -> dict[int, str]:
    """{pid: start time} of every live descendant of PID (a tool command codex ran in its own session is not in codex's process group), from one `ps`
    snapshot. The start time lets a later kill skip a pid that was reused by an unrelated process."""
    kids: dict[int, list[tuple[int, str]]] = {}
    for line in run(["ps", "-A", "-o", "pid=,ppid=,lstart="], timeout=20).stdout.splitlines():
        f = line.split(None, 2)
        if len(f) == 3 and f[0].isdigit() and f[1].isdigit():
            kids.setdefault(int(f[1]), []).append((int(f[0]), f[2].strip()))
    out: dict[int, str] = {}
    todo = [pid]
    while todo:
        for c, started in kids.get(todo.pop(), []):
            if c not in out:
                out[c] = started
                todo.append(c)
    return out


def alive_with_start(pid: int, started: str) -> bool:
    out = run(["ps", "-p", str(pid), "-o", "lstart="], timeout=20).stdout.strip()
    return out == started


def in_worktree(wt: Path) -> set[int]:
    """Pids whose working directory is inside WT (what is left of a tool that was reparented to init once its parent died): lsof, or /proc where there
    is no lsof (Linux)."""
    root, out = str(wt.resolve()), set()
    inside = lambda path: path == root or path.startswith(root + os.sep)
    if shutil.which("lsof"):
        pid = 0
        for line in run(["lsof", "-a", "-d", "cwd", "-Fpn"], timeout=60).stdout.splitlines():
            if line.startswith("p") and line[1:].isdigit():
                pid = int(line[1:])
            elif line.startswith("n") and inside(line[1:]) and pid != os.getpid():
                out.add(pid)
        return out
    for entry in Path("/proc").iterdir():
        if entry.name.isdigit() and int(entry.name) != os.getpid():
            try:
                if inside(os.readlink(entry / "cwd")):
                    out.add(int(entry.name))
            except OSError:
                pass
    return out


def kill_group(proc: subprocess.Popen, wt: Path, tracked: dict[int, str]) -> None:
    """SIGKILL everything of codex's: its process group, every descendant seen while it ran or now (TRACKED: tool commands run in sessions of their
    own, and are reparented once codex exits, so only a snapshot taken while it was alive finds one that works outside the worktree) and any process
    still working inside the review worktree; reap the parent."""
    mask_signals()    # the cleanup is not interruptible (Codex, PR 130 round 12)
    if proc.returncode is None:    # an unreaped leader: its group is still ours (a reaped pid may already belong to someone else)
        try:
            os.killpg(proc.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
        except (ProcessLookupError, PermissionError):
            pass
    victims: set[int] = set()
    try:
        for pid, started in {**tracked, **descendants(proc.pid)}.items():
            if alive_with_start(pid, started):
                victims.add(pid)
        victims |= in_worktree(wt)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        pass    # no ps / lsof: the group kill below is what remains
    for pid in victims:
        try:
            os.kill(pid, signal.SIGKILL)
        except (ProcessLookupError, PermissionError):
            pass
    try:
        proc.wait(timeout=10)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        pass


def finish(doc: dict, result_path: Path, t0: float, as_json: bool, usage_error: str | None = None) -> int:
    if usage_error:
        result_path.unlink(missing_ok=True)    # nothing was reviewed: no result file for a head that was never in scope
        return die(usage_error, EXIT_USAGE)
    doc["finished"] = now_iso()
    doc["elapsed_s"] = round(time.monotonic() - t0, 1)
    if doc["result"] != "failed":
        doc["reason"] = ""
    elif not doc["reason"]:
        doc["reason"] = "failed for an unrecorded reason"
    write_private(result_path, json.dumps(doc, indent=1) + "\n")
    c = doc["counts"]
    if doc["result"] == "clean":
        code, text = EXIT_CLEAN, "clean"
    elif doc["result"] == "findings":
        code = EXIT_FINDINGS
        text = "findings (" + ", ".join(f"{k} {c[k]}" for k in PRIORITIES if c[k]) + ")"
    else:
        code, text = EXIT_FAILED, f"FAILED: {doc['reason']}"
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps(doc, separators=(",", ":")))
    else:
        print(f"local-review PR {doc['pr']} at {doc['head'][:12]}: {text}; {doc['elapsed_s']} s; {result_path}")
        for f in doc["findings"]:
            print(f"  {f['priority']} {f['title']}" + (f" \u2014 {f['path']}" if f["path"] else ""))
        if doc["ignored_generated"]:
            print(f"  (ignored {len(doc['ignored_generated'])} finding(s) in generated hook files: {', '.join(GENERATED)})")
    if code == EXIT_FAILED:
        print(f"local-review: failed: {doc['reason']}", file=sys.stderr)
    return code


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as e:    # a preflight git or gh call: nothing was reviewed, which is a failure, never the "findings" exit 1
        sys.exit(die(f"{' '.join(map(str, e.cmd[:3]))} timed out before the review started", EXIT_FAILED))
    except FileNotFoundError as e:    # git or gh missing before there is any result to file
        sys.exit(die(f"{e.filename or 'a required program'} not found", EXIT_USAGE))
